    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "THIS CRIMINAL PETITION COMING ON FOR ADMISSION, THIS  DAY, ORDER WAS MADE THEREIN AS UNDER:\n -2-  NC: 2026:KHC-D:1580  CRL.P No. 101535 of 2021 HC-KAR  ORAL ORDER (PER: THE HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE V.SRISHANANDA) Learned counsel for the petitioner files a memo.\n2. Memo reads as under:\n\"Herein the Advocate for the Petitioner begs to submit as under:\nThat in the above case, the petitioners have challenged the FIR and complaint filed by the respondent No.1 with instigation of respondent No.2 bearing in Market P S Crime. No.67/2017 registered by the respondent for the alleged offences punishable under section 420, 465, 468, 467, 471, 464 of IPC- 1860 R/W Sections 436(A) of Karnataka Municipal Corporation Act, therefore the petitioners may kindly be permitted to withdraw the above petition and liberty may kindly reserve for the petitioner after filling of the charge sheet filed in Market P S Crime. No. 67/2017 and liberty to file the fresh petition, in the interest of justice and equity.\"\n3. Placing the memo on record, petition is dismissed as withdrawn with liberty as prayed for.\nSd/-\n(V.SRISHANANDA) JUDGE CLK CT:",
